      tz: "Ali ibn Yusuf's reign spanned the whole of the Almoravid empire, from the Sahara to central Spain. A pious ruler, he embellished the Qaraouiyine mosque in Fez, ordering its extension from eighteen to twenty-one aisles around 1135.\n\nHis later years were overshadowed by the Christian recovery — Zaragoza fell in 1118 — and by the rise of Ibn Tumart's Almohad movement in the Atlas from the 1120s. He died in 1143, and four years later Marrakech itself fell to the Almohads.",
