      tz: "Hassan I, a son of Mohammed IV, continued his father's reforms: a new army on the European model, and a series of administrative and tax reforms designed to strengthen the makhzen.\n\nAt the international level he defended Moroccan sovereignty at the Madrid Conference of 1880, and his travels through the country (the harkas) kept the tribes attached to the throne. He died in 1894, leaving the throne to his young son Abd al-Aziz.",
